  "body": "Found while checking zoecats' report (Discord #feedback, 10-25: a local aggregator answered \"quota exhausted\" while it switched upstreams; Try now in the provider's editor; only a restart brought answers back).\n\nWhen a key rests out of its allowance, magpie answers the next requests itself (quotaHeld, #1772) with `Retry-After` set to when the rest ends. In a sandbox on v0.1.1478, a single-key provider over a fake upstream answering 429 `{\"error\":{\"message\":\"quota exhausted\",\"type\":\"insufficient_quota\"}}` gave `Retry-After: 900` on both the upstream's 429 and magpie's held one.\n\nTry now (`POST /api/gateway/unrest`) lifts the rest in magpie: the next request reached the upstream and got 200 (checked on /v1/chat/completions and on /v1/messages, streaming and not). But an agent that honours the header waits up to 15 minutes before it sends that next request, so the user sees nothing change after Try now, and gives up and restarts.\n\nNot tried with a real harness: whether Claude Code, Codex or zoecats' harness waits on a Retry-After that long.\n\nOptions: keep the held reply's Retry-After short (the rest is magpie's, and a lift by hand can end it), or leave it and say on the Try now toast that an agent told to wait may still be waiting.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
